    "title": "C. Counting up across shards",
    "body": "**Part C: unique IDs.** With one database, **auto-increment** is simple: 1, 2, 3, in order, 8 bytes. After the photos are split into two shards (SD 8), each shard counts on its own: shard 1 and shard 2 both create photo **1001**. Giving each shard a separate range, or asking one central counter, fixes it, but every new ID then depends on that arrangement. Auto-increment IDs also tell anyone how many rows you create a day.",
