    "body": "A **random UUID** (version 4) has 122 random bits, so any server, or a phone while offline, can make one without asking anyone. Even after a billion IDs, the chance that two are equal is about 1 in 10¹⁹. But random IDs do not sort by time, and each new row lands at a random place in the database's index, touching pages all over it instead of only the last one. They are also 16 bytes instead of 8.",
